### T32 Dialog Change Detection

#### dialog opened

#### detects transition from idle to dialog

- Verify: detects transition from idle to dialog
   - Expected: changes.len() equals `1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract`
   - Expected: changes[0].change_type equals `dialog_opened`
   - Expected: changes[0].window_name equals `practice_dialog`
   - Expected: changes[0].old_value equals `idle`
   - Expected: changes[0].new_value equals `dialog`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 20 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: detects transition from idle to dialog")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-T32McpDial-001
val old_snap = T32DialogSnapshot(
    session_id: "s1",
    practice_state: "idle",
    items: [],
    window_names: []
)
val new_snap = T32DialogSnapshot(
    session_id: "s1",
    practice_state: "dialog",
    items: [],
    window_names: []
)
val changes = dialog_compute_changes(old_snap, new_snap)
expect(changes.len()).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
expect(changes[0].change_type).to_equal("dialog_opened")
expect(changes[0].window_name).to_equal("practice_dialog")
expect(changes[0].old_value).to_equal("idle")
expect(changes[0].new_value).to_equal("dialog")
```

</details>

